# Line endings are a repository property, not a per-developer one.
#
# `core.autocrlf` and `core.eol` are user-level settings, so without a rule
# here the terminator a blob ends up with depends on the machine it was
# committed from. The cost is silent diff inflation: every untouched line in
# such a file is rewritten with a different terminator, so a small edit is
# recorded as a rewrite and the real change disappears into it.
#
# The `mixed-line-ending` pre-commit hook does NOT enforce this on its own.
# Its default `--fix=auto` only acts on files that *mix* terminators, and
# normalises those to their own majority; a file that is consistently CRLF is
# not mixed, so the hook returns 0 without printing anything.
# `.pre-commit-config.yaml` pins `--fix=lf` so the hook enforces the same rule
# this file does.
#
# `text=auto` leaves git's binary detection in charge, so the .png and .whl
# fixtures are untouched; they are listed explicitly below anyway, because an
# explicit marker survives a future change to the detection heuristic.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.whl binary

# Map data is text and is normalised with everything else. Listed explicitly
# because these are large and a reviewer reaching for this file will want to
# see that the decision was made deliberately rather than by omission.
*.osm text eol=lf
*.xodr text eol=lf
